# Hardening freeze (HC-1)

Controlling plan: `docs/architecture/HARDENING_AND_RELEASE_ARCHITECTURE_PLAN.md`.
Decision: `docs/adr/0016-one-fact-one-state-one-eligibility-one-proof.md`.

Treat almost every new feature as secondary until the plan’s release-gate statements are true.

**Frozen:** new product surfaces, evidence semantics, Proof meaning, Enterprise modes, AI/CV, evidence-core redesign.

**Allowed:** named hardening defects, UX that removes local reasoning, tests, observability, release engineering, compatibility adapters.

```ts
// BAD — presentation invents workflow truth
resolveNextRequiredAction({ transaction, viewerId }); // protocol defaults to empty

// GOOD — application projection, required protocol, Proof availability from the Proof service
workspace.proof.availability === 'AVAILABLE'; // only then show View Proof
```

```ts
// BAD — transport calls eligibility / identity helpers
assertPassportEligible(transaction, records);
if (externalOrderId) authoritative = true;

// GOOD — ProofApplicationService after commerce+evidence load; trust from provenance
canAuthoritativelyBindOrder(source); // MERCHANT_SERVER_ATTESTED | PLATFORM_API_ATTESTED
```

P0 order: workspace projection → Proof application service → no lifecycle Proof readiness → Home/Portal consume the same object.

Do not claim `1.0.0`, `DEMO_READY`, or `LAUNCH_READY`. Do not commit `functions/.env.thepackproof-prod` or `google-services.production.local.json`.
